      "q": "15. Explain why passengers are thrown forward form their seats when a speeding bus stops suddenly.",
      "a": "When a fast bus comes to a complete stop, the bottom half of the body in touch with the seat comes to a complete halt, while the upper section of the passengers' bodies prefer to retain their uniform motion. As a result, the passengers are pushed forward."
