      "q": "6. Two bodies at different temperatures $${{\\mathbf{T}}_{\\mathbf{1}}}$$, and $${{\\mathbf{T}}_{\\mathbf{2}}}$$ are brought in thermal contact do not necessarily settle down to the mean temperature of $${{\\mathbf{T}}_{\\mathbf{1}}}$$ and $${{\\mathbf{T}}_{\\mathbf{2}}}$$\n.\nWhy?",
      "a": "When two bodies at different temperatures $${{\\mathbf{T}}_{\\mathbf{1}}}$$ and $${{\\mathbf{T}}_{\\mathbf{2}}}$$ are in thermal contact. They do not always settle at their mean temperature because the thermal capacities of two bodies may not always be equal."
