      "a": "Here, The Given:\n${{\\text{R}}_0} = $\nResistance at\n${0^0}{\\text{c}} = 2.56\\Omega $\n${{\\text{R}}_{\\text{t}}} = $\nResistance at temperature\n${\\text{T}} = {100^0}{\\text{c}} = 3.56\\Omega 100$\n${{\\text{R}}_{\\text{t}}} = $\nResistance at unknown temperature t;\n${{\\text{R}}_{\\text{t}}} = 5.06\\Omega $\nSince,\n${\\text{t}} = \\dfrac{{{R_t} - {R_0}}}{{{R_{100}} - {R_0}}} \\times 100$\n$ = \\dfrac{{(5.06 - 2.56)}}{{(3.56 - 2.56)}} \\times 100$\n$ = \\dfrac{{2.5 \\times 100}}{1}$\n$ = \\dfrac{{25}}{{10}} \\times 100$\n${\\text{t}} = {250^0}{\\text{c}}$"
