      "q": "43. From what height should a piece of ice fall so that it completely melts? Only one quarter of heat produced is absorbed by the ice. Given latent heat of ice is $3.4 \\times {10^5}\\;{\\text{J}}\\mid $ ${\\text{Kg}}$ and acceleration due to gravity, ${\\text{g}} = 10\\;{\\text{m}}\\mid {{\\text{s}}^2}$ ?",
      "a": "Let the Given,\n${\\text{m}} = $\nMass of piece of ice\n${\\text{h}}$\n= height from which it falls.\n$\\therefore $\nLoss of Potential energy\n$ = {\\text{mgh}}$\nThe Potential energy of ice is converted into heat.\nSince the ice absorbs only one - quarter of this,\n$\\therefore $\nHeat absorbed by ice,\n$Q = \\dfrac{1}{4}mgh \\to 1$\n)\nIf L Joules / Kg is the latent heat of ice, then\n$Q = mL \\to 2)$\nEquating 1) & 2) for Q\n$\\dfrac{1}{4}pgh = m2$\n$h = \\dfrac{{4L}}{g}$\n$h = \\dfrac{{4 \\times \\left( {3.4 \\times {{10}^5}} \\right)}}{{10}}$\n$h = 136 \\times {10^3}\\;{\\text{m}}$\n$h = 136{\\text{Km}}$"
