      "a": "(a) It is a stationary wave because the harmonic terms are present individually in the equation, the preceding equation indicates a stationary wave\n$kx$\nand\n$\\omega t$\nappear separately in the equation.\n(b) There is no harmonic term in the provided equation. As a result, it doesn't represent either a moving or stationary wave.\n(c) The harmonic terms in the preceding equation describe a moving wave and are in the combination of\n$kx$\nand\n$\\omega t$\nare in the combination of\n$kx - \\omega t$\n.\n(d) The given equation represents a stationary wave because the harmonic terms\n$kx$\nand\n$\\omega t$\nappear separately in the equation. This equation actually represents the superposition of two stationary waves."
