      "q": "20. Given two cases in which there is no Doppler effect in sound?",
      "a": "The two circumstances in which there is no Doppler effect in sound (i.e. no change in frequency) are as follows: -\n1) When both the sound source and the listener are moving in the same direction and at the same speed.\n2) When one of the source\u00a0 listeners is in the circle's center and the other is travelling around it at a constant speed."
